Package: hiermetacox
Type: Package
Title: Hierarchical Nonconvex Penalized Stratified Cox Models for Individual-Participant-Data Meta-Analysis
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Emmanuel", "Djegou", email = "emmanueldjegou5@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-5527-2301")),
    person("Bertin", "Dehigbe", role = "aut"),
    person("Jarrad", "Botchway", role = "aut"),
    person("Emmanuel", "Boamah", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits one-stage stratified Cox models for individual-participant-data
    (IPD) meta-analysis of time-to-event outcomes in which each study-specific
    log-hazard ratio is decomposed as a shared global effect plus a sparse
    study-specific deviation. Global effects and deviations are penalized by
    MCP, SCAD, lasso or elastic-net penalties with separate tuning parameters, a hierarchy
    constraint ensures that a covariate excluded globally is excluded in every
    study, and each study keeps its own unspecified baseline hazard. Includes a
    compiled coordinate-descent path algorithm, joint two-dimensional
    cross-validation with study-stratified folds, post-selection Wald
    inference, bootstrap selection stability, and a data generator for
    simulation studies.
